00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:53.140
Sort of that once in a lifetime.
算是那种一生只有一次的机会。

318
00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:54.700
Well, no, hopefully you'll have more.
嗯，不，希望你们以后还会有更多这样的机会。

319
00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:56.200
I don't know.
我不知道。

320
00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:58.860
I think it would be very hard to, I know another show.
我觉得很难再有另一部这样的剧了。

321
00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:01.700
We've both worked on other shows and you're right.
我们都参与过其他剧集，你是对的。

322
00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:03.040
It was lightning in a bottle.
那确实是可遇不可求的。

323
00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:06.560
We'll all go on to do other things, but this was a magical time for sure.
我们以后都会去做别的事情，但那段时光绝对是充满魔力的。

324
00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:07.600
It really was.
确实如此。

325
00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:08.000
Yeah.
是啊。

326
00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:09.660
Steve feels the same way for sure.
史蒂夫肯定也是这么想的。

327
00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:13.200
And that's why there's third graders with, you know, Dunder Mifflin shirts on.
这就是为什么现在还有三年级的小学生穿着邓德·米夫林的衬衫。

328
00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:14.000
That's right.
没错。

329
00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:18.160
Well, I have one last question for you.
好了，我还有一个问题要问你们。

330
00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:24.360
We always ask everyone if they took anything from the set before they left the show.
我们总是问每个人，在离开剧组之前有没有从片场拿走什么东西。

331
00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:28.660
Now, I don't know collectively if you and Steve have something from the set.
现在，我不知道你和史蒂夫是不是一起从片场拿了什么东西。

332
00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:32.080
I mean, Jen and I, obviously we've shared this.
我是说，珍和我，显然我们分享过这个。

333
00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:33.100
We took a lot of things.
我们拿了很多东西。

334
00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:39.380
I so want you to say that you took like the for sale sign from the lawn, the finale, but
我真希望你说你拿走了大结局里草坪上的那个“待售”标志，但是

335
00:14:39.380 --> 00:14:41.580
I'm sure that would be a very odd thing.
我敢肯定那会是一件很奇怪的事情。

336
00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:45.820
If you're just pulling it out of the ground, be like, I'm taking this.
如果你只是把它从地里拔出来，然后说，我要拿走这个。

337
00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:47.620
Just throwing it in my car.
直接扔进我的车里。

338
00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:51.120
You know what?
你知道吗？

339
00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:51.680
No.
没有。

340
00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:54.840
I don't think Steve took one thing.
我觉得史蒂夫什么都没拿。

341
00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:56.280
Wow.
哇。

342
00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:57.940
We're going to follow up.
我们会跟进调查的。

343
00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.200
Guess what you're going to have.
猜猜你会得到什么。

344
00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:01.700
You're going to have a Christmas ornament of that postcard.
你会得到一个那张明信片的圣诞装饰品。

345
00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:04.680
That'll be your little nod.
那将是你的一点小纪念。

346
00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:06.380
Yeah.
是啊。

347
00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:07.820
No, I don't think he took anything.
不，我觉得他什么都没拿。

348
00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:10.280
I remember, do you remember his last day?
我记得，你还记得他最后一天吗？

349
00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:13.140
I mean, I just remember crying a lot.
我是说，我只记得当时哭得很厉害。

350
00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:13.400
Yeah.
是啊。

351
00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:19.120
The big party and then they made him a huge coffee cup cake that said world's best boss.
那场盛大的派对，他们还给他做了一个巨大的咖啡杯蛋糕，上面写着“世界最佳老板”。

352
00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:20.360
I do remember that.
我记得那件事。

353
00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:23.300
And then you guys all signed a hockey jersey.
然后你们大家还在一件冰球衫上签了名。

354
00:15:23.720 --> 00:15:24.140
Yeah.
是啊。

355
00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:24.900
For him.
送给他的。

356
00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:26.540
Like, so we have all that stuff.
总之，我们留着所有那些东西。

357
00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:31.580
You know, we have that framed and we have that up, but not the coffee cup cake.
你知道，我们把那些东西装裱起来挂着，但咖啡杯蛋糕没留着。

358
00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:33.500
We ate that.
我们把它吃了。

359
00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:33.800
Yeah.
是啊。

360
00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:34.560
Yeah, we ate that.
没错，我们把它吃了。

361
00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:38.920
But so we have stuff like that, but no, he never took like, you know, his anything.
所以我们确实留着这类东西，但他没有，他从来没带走过他的任何东西。

362
00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:40.000
Wow.
哇。

363
00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:45.100
I would think he would have like his Dundee from his desk or something.
我本以为他会带走桌上的邓迪奖杯之类的东西。

364
00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:45.940
I don't know.
我不知道。

365
00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:46.660
You know what?
你知道吗？

366
00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:47.120
Not even that.
连那个都没带。

367
00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:48.400
He's too classy.
他太有格调了。

368
00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:50.020
He's too classy, Jenna.
他太有格调了，珍娜。

369
00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:53.940
He didn't rob the set on his way out like the rest of us were againSt.
他离开时没有像我们其他人那样洗劫片场。

370
00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:55.620
We're like, is that nailed down?
我们当时都在想，那个钉牢了吗？

371
00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:56.400
It's going with me.
我要把它带走。

372
00:15:56.400 --> 00:16:00.640
Well, maybe he thought he wasn't, he probably wasn't sure if like anybody was going to need
嗯，也许他当时不确定，他可能不确定是否还有人会需要它，

373
00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.500
it again because, you know.
因为，你知道的。

374
00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:03.660
Well, that's true, right?
嗯，那倒是真的，对吧？

375
00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:05.340
Because the show kept going.
因为剧集还在继续。

376
00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:07.920
So you kind of couldn't.
所以你没法那样做。

377
00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:08.400
Yeah.
是啊。

378
00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:09.120
Could you imagine?
你能想象吗？

379
00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.440
We're like, where'd the Dunder Mifflin sign go?
我们当时会想，邓德·米夫林的招牌去哪了？

380
00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:12.300
Steve took it.
史蒂夫拿走了。

381
00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:13.080
No one's seen it.
没人见过它。

382
00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:14.080
Steve left.
史蒂夫离开了。

383
00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:17.740
Where'd the desk go in Michael's office?
迈克尔办公室里的桌子去哪了？

384
00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:18.120
Huh?
啊？

385
00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:20.340
He stole everything.
他把一切都偷走了。

386
00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:25.840
Oh, Nancy, thank you so much for coming on and talking with us.
噢，南希，非常感谢你来和我们聊天。

387
00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:29.900
You were such a big part of the show, both on camera and behind the scenes.
无论是在镜头前还是幕后，你都是这部剧非常重要的一部分。

388
00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:36.540
We just have the best memories of you coming to set either with your family or as Carol.
你带着家人或者以卡罗尔的身份来到片场，我们对这些记忆犹新。

389
00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:37.940
This was so great.
这真是太棒了。

390
00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:39.040
Thanks, you guys.
谢谢你们。

391
00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.900
I too have the best memories.
我也拥有最美好的回忆。

392
00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:47.060
That was, that show was a joy and everybody involved with it was just incredible.
那部剧真是一段快乐的时光，参与其中的每个人都太棒了。

393
00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:51.300
And it was a real privilege to be on that show and to know you guys.
能参演那部剧并认识你们，真是我的荣幸。

394
00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:52.940
We feel the same way.
我们也有同感。

395
00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.100
You know, BJ Novak said something to me recently.
你知道，BJ·诺瓦克最近跟我说了些话。

396
00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:57.340
He was like, Angela, it's office family forever.
他说，安吉拉，办公室大家庭永远在一起。

397
00:16:57.640 --> 00:16:58.680
We're family forever.
我们永远是一家人。

398
00:16:58.920 --> 00:16:59.500
It's true.
这是真的。

399
00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:00.500
It's like, it's so true.
没错，真是太对了。

400
00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:02.040
We love you.
我们爱你。

401
00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:02.880
We love you.
我们爱你。

402
00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:03.980
I love you too.
我也爱你。

403
00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:17.710
I just kind of need Nancy to be another office ladies and hang out with us all the time.
我只是觉得南希应该成为我们办公室女郎的一员，一直和我们待在一起。

404
00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:19.210
I agree.
我同意。

405
00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:20.470
Can we make that happen?
我们能实现这个愿望吗？

406
00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:22.810
How much texting to her is too much?
给她发多少短信才算太多？

407
00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:24.370
I don't know.
我不知道。

408
00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:26.570
I feel like we blew up her phone lately.
我觉得我们最近把她的手机都快轰炸了。

409
00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:28.570
Well, let's get into this episode.
好吧，让我们进入这一集的内容吧。

410
00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:30.190
Let's do that, lady.
好的，女士。

411
00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:32.890
Is anyone else out there watching the DVDs?
还有人在看DVD吗？

412
00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:33.450
Anyone?
有人吗？

413
00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:34.450
Let me know.
告诉我一声。

414
00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:38.290
Because did you notice this disc is full of so many ads?
因为你们有没有注意到这张光盘里全是广告？

415
00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:39.250
It is?
是吗？

416
00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:43.770
You have to sit through all these commercials for other things done by Universal Studios.
你得看完所有这些环球影业其他作品的商业广告。

417
00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:47.130
And I'm just like, I can quote The Big Lebowski to you now.
我当时就想，我现在都能背出《谋杀绿脚趾》的台词了。

418
00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:52.110
The Big Lebowski, the movie, was being promoted on the Office DVD?
《谋杀绿脚趾》这部电影在《办公室》的DVD里做宣传？

419
00:17:52.350 --> 00:17:52.790
Yes.
是的。

420
00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:57.830
Especially on this disc for season seven.
特别是在第七季的这张光盘上。

421
00:17:58.330 --> 00:18:02.790
You guys know, you folks out there watching it, it's like Parks and Rec, and then all of
你们知道的，在座各位正在看的朋友们，就像《公园与游憩》一样，然后突然间，

422
00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:03.690
a sudden, The Big Lebowski.
就变成了《谋杀绿脚趾》。

423
00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:05.370
That's crazy.
太疯狂了。

424
00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:07.810
Anyway, I'm just saying, a lot of ads on this one.
总之，我只是说，这一张里的广告特别多。

425
00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:12.570
Let's talk about this cold open, because Dwight has gone up to some kind of hardware store
我们来聊聊这个开场戏，因为德怀特去了一家五金店，

426
00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:17.370
where there's day laborers, they're looking for a job, and he's pulled up and he's asking
那里有零工在找工作，他开车过去，问

427
00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:19.190
someone to come with him to work.
有没有人愿意跟他去干活。

428
00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:24.450
Yes, but no one will go, and we find out why.
是的，但没人愿意去，我们知道了原因。

429
00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:31.590
An older worker explains that no one goes with this man, this man being Dwight.
一位年长的工人解释说，没人愿意跟这个人走，这个人指的就是德怀特。

430
00:18:31.730 --> 00:18:32.110
That's right.
没错。

431
00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:35.030
Because when they go with him, they never come back.
因为只要跟了他，就再也没回来过。

432
00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:35.410
Yeah.
是啊。

433
00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:36.630
It's a mystery.
这真是一个谜。

434
00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.330
So they're not going with him anymore.
所以他们再也不跟他走了。

435
00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:38.870
No.
没错。

436
00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:44.070
The man who's explaining all of this to us in Spanish is Abraham Chavez, and the boy
用西班牙语向我们解释这一切的人是亚伯拉罕·查韦斯，而那个

437
00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:46.850
who is interpreting is Oscar Blanco.
负责翻译的男孩是奥斯卡·布兰科。

438
00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:49.410
Neither of them have been on Monk or House.
他们俩都没演过《神探阿蒙》或《豪斯医生》。

439
00:18:49.590 --> 00:18:51.010
Oh, you don't get to do your house pun.
噢，你没法玩你的“豪斯”双关语了。

440
00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:51.630
I don't.
确实没法玩了。

441
00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:52.650
Guests are in the house.
嘉宾们在屋里（house）。

442
00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:55.850
I mean, spoiler alert, I'm not going to get to do it all episode.
我是说，剧透预警，我这一整集都没法玩这个梗了。

443
00:18:56.750 --> 00:18:58.070
I'm bummed, but it's okay.
我很沮丧，但没关系。

444
00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:01.190
Well, in this cold open, we are going to meet Nate.
好吧，在这个开场戏里，我们要见到内特了。

445
00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:02.970
He approaches Dwight's car.
他走向德怀特的车。

446
00:19:03.170 --> 00:19:06.110
They speak terrible Spanish to one another.
他们用蹩脚的西班牙语互相交流。

447
00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:08.730
And Dwight is like, all right, you can work for me today.
德怀特说，好吧，你今天可以为我工作。

448
00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:09.290
Hop in.
上车吧。

449
00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:10.070
Yeah.
是啊。

450
00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:15.410
He's going to bring him to our parking lot where he asks him to, I guess, get a hornet's
他要把他带到我们的停车场，我猜是让他去处理一个马蜂窝

451
00:19:15.410 --> 00:19:16.230
nest out of a tree.
树上的巢。

452
00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:16.890
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

453
00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:17.530
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

454
00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:19.870
He's going to give him a few ways to do that.
他打算给他提供几种处理方法。

455
00:19:19.990 --> 00:19:21.970
Blow torch, bow and arrow, bat.
喷灯、弓箭、球棒。

456
00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:22.990
There's a few options.
有几种选择。

457
00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:23.910
Yeah.
是啊。

458
00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:25.070
Yeah, it's kind of a teSt.
没错，这算是一种测试。

459
00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:28.850
He ultimately chooses the bat.
他最终选择了球棒。

460
00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:29.670
Yeah.
是啊。

461
00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:31.010
Bad idea.
坏主意。

462
00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:33.450
The whole bullpen has gathered around to watch this.
整个牛棚的人都围过来观看这一幕。

463
00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:35.570
They're very invested, worried.
他们非常投入，也很担心。

464
00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:36.850
There's highs, there's lows.
有起有落。

465
00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:39.530
It's a really high energy moment for the group.
这对团队来说是一个情绪非常高涨的时刻。

466
00:19:39.930 --> 00:19:45.150
And Randy shared with us that at a minute, seven seconds, when you see that establishing
兰迪和我们分享说，在视频一分零七秒时，当你看到那个内特在停车场的定场镜头时，

467
00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:50.150
shot of Nate in the parking lot, all of those shots were from Greg Daniels' office window.
所有这些镜头都是从格雷格·丹尼尔斯的办公室窗户拍的。

468
00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:51.630
That's right.
没错。

469
00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:52.130
Yeah.
是啊。

470
00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:55.850
But the cast was actually in our conference room set.
但演员们其实是在我们的会议室布景里。

471
00:19:55.950 --> 00:19:56.270
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

472
00:19:56.370 --> 00:20:00.410
And I remember when we were shooting that, that our first AD was calling out the Nate
我记得拍摄的时候，我们的第一副导演在喊内特的

473
00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:00.770
action.
动作指令。

474
00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:02.210
We couldn't actually see him.
我们其实根本看不见他。

475
00:20:02.350 --> 00:20:03.410
We were looking at nothing.
我们什么也没看着。

476
00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:05.090
We were looking at a scrim.
我们对着一块幕布。

477
00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:05.550
Yeah.
是啊。

478
00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:06.750
Just a screen.
就一个屏幕。

479
00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:07.550
Painted backdrop.
画出来的背景。

480
00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:11.550
And we were pretending to react to all the different things they were saying.
我们假装对他们说的各种话做出反应。

481
